{"content_hash": "5f21948f3cc16aa9", "version_id": 425, "article_id": 43, "level_code": "en_c1", "lang": "en", "level": 5, "level_label": "C1 高级", "title": "NHS waiting list grows as 'ominous signs' of winter pressure hit", "title_zh": "NHS候诊名单再度攀升，冬季压力“不祥信号”已现", "has_translation": true, "topic": "health", "source": "bbc_health", "source_url": "https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/cxnv03e9nmp4o?at_medium=RSS&at_campaign=rss", "image": {"type": "photo", "url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1540683153640-c28d7f6810f0?ixid=M3wxMDk3Mzk1fDB8MXxzZWFyY2h8N3x8b21pbm91cyUyMHNpZ25zJTIwd2ludGVyfGVufDB8MHx8fDE3OTE1OTQ0Mzd8MA&ixlib=rb-4.1.0&w=1600&q=75&fm=jpg&fit=max", "provider": "unsplash", "credit": "Photo by Shawn Bagley on Unsplash", "author": "Shawn Bagley", "credit_url": "https://unsplash.com/@utahdesertguy?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "source": "Unsplash", "source_url": "https://unsplash.com/photos/road-sign-near-pine-trees-bUADDFi1Qs0?utm_source=daily-english-news&utm_medium=referral", "fallback": {"type": "gradient", "from": "hsl(352, 42%, 62%)", "to": "hsl(30, 46%, 48%)", "label": "HEALTH", "seed": "b128cdf1738d"}}, "published_date": "2026-10-08", "word_count": 211, "reading_minutes": 1.1, "lead": "Fresh data shows the NHS waiting list in England has risen for a second month, prompting warnings that winter pressures are already building. Health leaders fear the government's 18-week treatment target is slipping out of reach.", "lead_zh": "最新数据显示，英格兰NHS候诊名单已连续第二个月上升，引发警告称冬季压力已在积聚。卫生领导人担心，政府提出的18周治疗目标正变得遥不可及。", "preview": "The waiting list for routine hospital treatment in England has grown for a second consecutive month, with an estimated 7.37 million treatmen", "preview_zh": "英格兰常规住院治疗的候诊名单已连续第二个月增长，截至8月底估计有737万项治疗待进行，为2025年10月以来的最高水平。这令人怀疑NHS能否实现政府承诺——到2029年让92%的患者在18周内得到治疗。", "has_audio": true, "audio": {"id": 415, "url": "https://pub-aba43a6fb1db4dc08fede1dbc81f3241.r2.dev/audio/43/en_c1.mp3", "duration": 88.088, "size_bytes": 532224, "engine": "edge-tts", "voice": "en-US-AriaNeural", "word_count": 240, "has_timeline": true}, "detail_url": "https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/gh/chjam12301-sys/news-etl@fc48a26/content/data/versions/425.json", "paragraphs": ["The waiting list for routine hospital treatment in England has grown for a second consecutive month, with an estimated 7.37 million treatments pending at the end of August — the highest since October 2025. This has cast doubt on whether the NHS can meet the government's pledge to treat 92% of patients within 18 weeks by 2029.", "The rise came despite record levels of planned care over the summer, when 4.7 million treatments and appointments were delivered across June, July and August. Yet A&Es and ambulance services also saw record demand in September, with more patients arriving with flu and respiratory viruses than is usual for the time of year.", "NHS England medical director Professor Frankie Swords warned that staff were already seeing 'ominous early signs of pressure'. Health Secretary Yvette Cooper praised frontline staff but urged eligible people to get flu jabs, while the NHS Alliance said the government would not hit its 18-week target by 2029.", "Analysis by the Health Foundation found progress on waiting times had stalled, with referrals rising faster than treatments. In September, 74.4% of A&E patients were seen within four hours, down from 75.0% in August, and 50,582 people waited over 12 hours from a decision to admit to admission — a 13% year-on-year rise."], "paragraphs_zh": ["英格兰常规住院治疗的候诊名单已连续第二个月增长，截至8月底估计有737万项治疗待进行，为2025年10月以来的最高水平。这令人怀疑NHS能否实现政府承诺——到2029年让92%的患者在18周内得到治疗。", "尽管夏季的计划性护理达到创纪录水平——6月至8月共完成470万项治疗和预约，候诊名单仍上升。但9月急诊和救护车服务也创下需求纪录，因流感和呼吸道病毒就诊的患者比往年同期更多。", "英格兰NHS医疗总监弗兰基·斯沃兹教授警告称，员工已看到“不祥的早期压力迹象”。卫生大臣伊薇特·库珀赞扬了一线员工，但敦促符合条件者接种流感疫苗；NHS联盟则表示政府无法在2029年前实现18周目标。", "健康基金会的分析发现，缩短候诊时间的进展已停滞，转诊速度超过治疗速度。9月，74.4%的急诊患者在四小时内就诊，低于8月的75.0%；50582人从决定收治到实际入院等待超过12小时，同比上升13%。"], "body": "The waiting list for routine hospital treatment in England has grown for a second consecutive month, with an estimated 7.37 million treatments pending at the end of August — the highest since October 2025. This has cast doubt on whether the NHS can meet the government's pledge to treat 92% of patients within 18 weeks by 2029.\n\nThe rise came despite record levels of planned care over the summer, when 4.7 million treatments and appointments were delivered across June, July and August. Yet A&Es and ambulance services also saw record demand in September, with more patients arriving with flu and respiratory viruses than is usual for the time of year.\n\nNHS England medical director Professor Frankie Swords warned that staff were already seeing 'ominous early signs of pressure'. Health Secretary Yvette Cooper praised frontline staff but urged eligible people to get flu jabs, while the NHS Alliance said the government would not hit its 18-week target by 2029.\n\nAnalysis by the Health Foundation found progress on waiting times had stalled, with referrals rising faster than treatments. In September, 74.4% of A&E patients were seen within four hours, down from 75.0% in August, and 50,582 people waited over 12 hours from a decision to admit to admission — a 13% year-on-year rise.", "body_zh": "英格兰常规住院治疗的候诊名单已连续第二个月增长，截至8月底估计有737万项治疗待进行，为2025年10月以来的最高水平。这令人怀疑NHS能否实现政府承诺——到2029年让92%的患者在18周内得到治疗。\n\n尽管夏季的计划性护理达到创纪录水平——6月至8月共完成470万项治疗和预约，候诊名单仍上升。但9月急诊和救护车服务也创下需求纪录，因流感和呼吸道病毒就诊的患者比往年同期更多。\n\n英格兰NHS医疗总监弗兰基·斯沃兹教授警告称，员工已看到“不祥的早期压力迹象”。卫生大臣伊薇特·库珀赞扬了一线员工，但敦促符合条件者接种流感疫苗；NHS联盟则表示政府无法在2029年前实现18周目标。\n\n健康基金会的分析发现，缩短候诊时间的进展已停滞，转诊速度超过治疗速度。9月，74.4%的急诊患者在四小时内就诊，低于8月的75.0%；50582人从决定收治到实际入院等待超过12小时，同比上升13%。", "text": "The waiting list for routine hospital treatment in England has grown for a second consecutive month, with an estimated 7.37 million treatments pending at the end of August — the highest since October 2025. This has cast doubt on whether the NHS can meet the government's pledge to treat 92% of patients within 18 weeks by 2029. The rise came despite record levels of planned care over the summer, when 4.7 million treatments and appointments were delivered across June, July and August. Yet A&Es and ambulance services also saw record demand in September, with more patients arriving with flu and respiratory viruses than is usual for the time of year. NHS England medical director Professor Frankie Swords warned that staff were already seeing 'ominous early signs of pressure'. Health Secretary Yvette Cooper praised frontline staff but urged eligible people to get flu jabs, while the NHS Alliance said the government would not hit its 18-week target by 2029. Analysis by the Health Foundation found progress on waiting times had stalled, with referrals rising faster than treatments. In September, 74.4% of A&E patients were seen within four hours, down from 75.0% in August, and 50,582 people waited over 12 hours from a decision to admit to admission — a 13% year-on-year rise.", "vocab": [{"word": "ominous", "pos": "adj", "zh": "不祥的，预示凶兆的", "note": "常与signs、warning等搭配，暗示坏事即将发生"}, {"word": "waiting list", "pos": "noun", "zh": "候诊名单", "note": "英式英语中特指NHS等待治疗的患者名单"}, {"word": "routine", "pos": "adj", "zh": "常规的，例行的", "note": "routine treatment指非紧急的常规治疗"}, {"word": "elective care", "pos": "noun", "zh": "择期护理", "note": "指计划内、非紧急的医疗程序"}, {"word": "A&E", "pos": "noun", "zh": "急诊室", "note": "Accident & Emergency的缩写，英式用法"}, {"word": "respiratory", "pos": "adj", "zh": "呼吸系统的", "note": "respiratory viruses指呼吸道病毒"}, {"word": "pledge", "pos": "noun", "zh": "承诺，誓言", "note": "常指政治或正式的保证"}, {"word": "referral", "pos": "noun", "zh": "转诊", "note": "全科医生将患者转给专科医生的过程"}, {"word": "stall", "pos": "verb", "zh": "停滞，搁浅", "note": "指进展停止，常与progress搭配"}, {"word": "corridor care", "pos": "noun", "zh": "走廊护理", "note": "指患者因床位不足在走廊接受治疗"}, {"word": "year-on-year", "pos": "adj/adv", "zh": "与去年同期相比的", "note": "用于比较年度数据变化"}, {"word": "relentless", "pos": "adj", "zh": "持续不断的，无情的", "note": "形容增长或压力毫不减弱"}, {"word": "disruption", "pos": "noun", "zh": "中断，扰乱", "note": "常指服务或计划受到干扰"}, {"word": "vulnerable", "pos": "adj", "zh": "脆弱的，易受伤害的", "note": "指需要保护的人群，如老人、病人"}], "title_original": "'Ominous signs' of winter pressures as NHS waiting list grows", "summary_original": "NHS winter pressures appear to be building already, with rises in waiting times for planned surgery.", "body_original": "'Ominous signs' of winter pressures as NHS waiting list grows\nBy\nDominic Hughes\nHealth correspondent\nPublished\n8 October 2026\nThere are \"ominous signs\" that winter pressures are already affecting the NHS in England, according to senior health leaders.\nThe warning comes as new data reveals the waiting list for routine hospital treatment in England rose for the second month in a row.\nAn estimated 7.37 million treatments were waiting to be carried out at the end of August, relating to 6.24 million patients.\nThe numbers are the highest since October 2025 and have raised questions over whether the NHS will meet a government target of treating 92% of patients within 18 weeks by 2029.\nThe rise in waiting lists comes despite the NHS in England delivering what were described as record levels of planned, elective care over the summer, while demand for services also reached its highest level ever.\nA record 4.7 million planned treatments, procedures and appointments occurred across June, July and August – more than in any previous summer.\nBut both A&Es and ambulance services also saw a record number of patients for the month of September.\nNHS England's national medical director, Professor Frankie Swords, warned that despite the progress delivered by frontline teams, winter pressure was already building.\n\"Staff are already seeing the ominous early signs of pressure, with more patients coming to A&E with flu and other respiratory viruses than usual for this time of year, and unfortunately many people are still waiting longer than we would like them to,\" she said.\nHealth and Social Care Secretary, Yvette Cooper said the NHS has been dealing with summer pressures as well as winter pressures.\n\"It is a huge tribute to doctors, nurses and staff across the NHS that alongside dealing with unprecedented levels of A&E attendances and ambulance call-outs, they also managed to deliver record numbers of elective appointments, procedures and treatments.\n\"Step by step, our NHS has been increasing its delivery and performance, making a real difference to patients' lives even as demand is growing.\n\"But with winter now approaching, pressure on our NHS is set to increase again and I would encourage everyone who is eligible for the flu jab and other vaccines to get themselves protected against preventable illnesses, and help relieve the workload on the NHS too.\"\n\"Relentless growth in demand for care\"\nThe NHS Alliance, which represents hospitals, says the government in England is not going to achieve its manifesto promise of hitting the 18-week hospital waiting time target by the end of the parliament in 2029.\nThat 18-week target hasn't been hit for a decade.\nA separate analysis by the Health Foundation think-tank said progress on cutting waiting times had stalled over the past year, with referrals on to the waiting list rising at a much quicker rate than the number of patients being treated.\nSir Ciarán Devane, the chief executive of the NHS Alliance which represents NHS trusts, said: \"The NHS continues to respond to record demand for care, but the relentless growth in demand for services is putting NHS staff under real pressure.\"\nFrancesca Cavallaro, of the Health Foundation, said: \"Thanks to the hard work of staff, the NHS has made progress in bringing down waiting times, but a rise in referrals mean that the service is having to run faster just to stand still and the prospects of meeting the government's pledge are receding.\n\"Andy Burnham's government have yet to set out whether they will give the 18-week target the same priority as it had under Keir Starmer, but our analysis shows the pledge is becoming increasingly hard to deliver.\"\n\"Not just numbers, but vulnerable people\"\nThere will be concern too that the pressures of a long, hot summer have merged almost seamlessly into the pressures associated with the winter months.\nMore patients, including children, have been arriving at A&E departments with flu and other respiratory viruses.\nThe number of patients seen within four hours in A&Es last month fell to 74.4%, down from 75.0% in August.\nThe number of people waiting more than 12 hours in A&E departments from a decision to admit to actually being admitted – what is known as \"corridor care\" – stood at 50,582 in September, up from 44,951 in August.\nThat has alarmed Dr Vicky Price, president of the Society for Acute Medicine.\n\"A 13% year-on-year rise in 12-hour emergency department waits as winter approaches should set alarm bells ringing.\n\"More than 50,000 patients waited over 12 hours from the decision to admit to admission in September - 1,686 people every day.\n\"These are not just numbers.\n\"They represent vulnerable people who are waiting far too long for a bed and staff trying to deliver safe care in overcrowded emergency departments.\"\nThe government says the 18-week mark could still be achieved, saying it was investing in NHS buildings and equipment to make services more productive.\nIt also pointed to disruption to care that was caused by the strikes by resident doctors, a dispute which has now been settled.\nBut the strain that services are feeling in September, before winter has even really got going, will be a cause for concern among NHS leaders and their political bosses alike.\nGet in touch\nHave you been on an NHS waiting list for a long time? Share your experience\nContact form\nContact form\nRelated topics\nNHS\nEngland\nHealth\nNHS England\nWaiting times\nMore on this story\nRise in people waiting for NHS treatment for fourth month in a row\nPublished\n17 September\nFears of two-tier health system as more turn to private care, says watchdog\nPublished\n16 March\nI'm on six different NHS waiting lists - it's taking over my life\nPublished\n23 April", "fetched_at": "2026-10-10T01:07:16.505883", "timeline": [{"i": 0, "w": "The", "s": 0.1, "e": 0.275, "sm": 100, "em": 275, "cs": 0, "ce": 3, "si": 0}, {"i": 1, "w": "waiting", "s": 0.287, "e": 0.625, "sm": 287, "em": 625, "cs": 4, "ce": 11, "si": 0}, {"i": 2, "w": "list", "s": 0.637, "e": 0.962, "sm": 637, "em": 962, "cs": 12, "ce": 16, "si": 0}, {"i": 3, "w": "for", "s": 0.975, "e": 1.113, "sm": 975, "em": 1112, "cs": 17, "ce": 20, "si": 0}, {"i": 4, "w": "routine", "s": 1.125, "e": 1.525, "sm": 1125, "em": 1525, "cs": 21, "ce": 28, "si": 0}, {"i": 5, "w": "hospital", "s": 1.538, "e": 2.025, "sm": 1537, "em": 2025, "cs": 29, "ce": 37, "si": 0}, {"i": 6, "w": "treatment", "s": 2.038, "e": 2.462, "sm": 2037, "em": 2462, "cs": 38, "ce": 47, "si": 0}, {"i": 7, "w": "in", "s": 2.475, "e": 2.587, "sm": 2475, "em": 2587, "cs": 48, "ce": 50, "si": 0}, {"i": 8, "w": "England", "s": 2.6, "e": 2.975, "sm": 2600, "em": 2975, "cs": 51, "ce": 58, "si": 0}, {"i": 9, "w": "has", "s": 2.987, "e": 3.175, "sm": 2987, "em": 3175, "cs": 59, "ce": 62, "si": 0}, {"i": 10, "w": "grown", "s": 3.188, "e": 3.525, "sm": 3187, "em": 3525, "cs": 63, "ce": 68, "si": 0}, {"i": 11, "w": "for", "s": 3.538, "e": 3.7, "sm": 3537, "em": 3700, "cs": 69, "ce": 72, "si": 0}, {"i": 12, "w": "a", "s": 3.712, "e": 3.775, "sm": 3712, "em": 3775, "cs": 73, "ce": 74, "si": 0}, {"i": 13, "w": "second", "s": 3.788, "e": 4.162, "sm": 3787, "em": 4162, "cs": 75, "ce": 81, "si": 0}, {"i": 14, "w": "consecutive", "s": 4.175, "e": 4.737, "sm": 4175, "em": 4737, "cs": 82, "ce": 93, "si": 0}, {"i": 15, "w": "month", "s": 4.75, "e": 5.1, "sm": 4750, "em": 5100, "cs": 94, "ce": 99, "si": 0}, {"i": 16, "w": ",", "s": 5.1, "e": 5.45, "sm": 5100, "em": 5450, "cs": 99, "ce": 100, "si": 0}, {"i": 17, "w": "with", "s": 5.45, "e": 5.6, "sm": 5450, "em": 5600, "cs": 101, "ce": 105, "si": 